 - Beautified the **Diplomacy Screen**'s **trading rows** with **icons** (e.g., Gold, Gold Per Turn, World Map, Open Borders, Vassal, Defensive Pact; and **leader icons** (make peace / declare war / embargo)). Change in `CvPlayer::getItemTradeString`. See [README.md: Diplomacy Screen](/README.md#diplomacy-screen).
 - **Main Interface (Common)**: Moved **minimap to the right-edge** for quicker read. Add **details** to most **progress bars**; e.g. in the Tech bar `Fusion: 2245 / 5774 (35)`. Show **chars in the GP bar even if 100%** (e.g. `Great Scientist: Lyons (3) - [RESEARCH_CHAR] 100%`) Change in [GPUtil.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/GPUtil.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). **Swap top left** (e.g., Treasury) **and top right** (e.g., Turn and Year) **text position**, and optionally **move commerce sliders to the right side** (allows to freely expand advisors so they use the entire left side, and is visually closer to scoreboard and most mouse controls) **in city screen or map view**. **Reduce commerce sliders fast increment** (`++ and --` optional buttons ("Min/Max Buttons in BUG Menu")) from **100 to 50** and make them **tunable**. When **Min/Max commerce buttons** are enabled in **map view**, move the green commerce rate values (e.g. `+297/Turn`) into a **compact row below the sliders** (e.g. `[RESEARCH_CHAR]297; [ESPIONAGE_CHAR]16`) so the slider block can be shifted right enough to keep both the **percentage text** and the **Min/Max buttons** visible near expanded advisors such as the Technology Advisor, while avoiding right-edge overflow in normal map view too. Show **Era text default ON** (as of now on top left); **strip " Era" suffix** so text is now only e.g., `Renaissance` not `Renaissance Era` (would overflow during golden age when text is upscaled, plus it is unneeded). See [Main interface rework](/README.md#main-interface-rework).
 - **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** (with optional separate blue ribbon, bar Y position and bar height position fine-tuning tunables (e.g., helps remove needless scroll bar when there are not more than max rows, or keep display symmetric or prettier)) and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Add **redirect to Sevopedia on click** (preserving `WIDGET_HELP` hover) for **Religion** and **Corporation** icons. Add a tunable **city bonus panel render mode**: **mode 0** keeps the old AdvCiv-SAS text glyphs (Civ4's `screen.setLabelAt`: smaller; also used as overflow fallback), **mode 1** uses base AdvCiv-style framed image buttons (Civ4's `setImageButton`) but now with **larger icons** when there is room, and **mode 2** uses frameless DDS rendering (Civ4's `addDDS`) with the same larger-size logic for a cleaner look. Active non-obsolete **Bonus** icons can open Sevopedia too (mode 0 text glyphs did not redirect to Sevopedia in testing; mode 1: left/right click; mode 2: right click only in our Python-only attempts so far). Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only") and restored **Production Chooser Bar** row-jump buttons with clearer hover text ("Scroll to Units/Buildings/Wonders"). Reduce **food/production top bars' size** so text does not overflow when upscaled (also helps preserve overall distance to side panels due to increasing base font size from body to label). Add **commerce sliders fast increment buttons** (`++ and --` optional buttons ("Min/Max Buttons in BUG Menu")) in city screen (matching the ones in map view) (not added in Finance Tab or Espionage Tab because these still have access to commerce sliders as of now at their right in map view). Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). Adjust **city camera** to the north (tunable) so extra rows can be shown without overflowing into bottom BFC plots in `CvGame::onCityScreenChange`. And other changes. See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemingly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
-- **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. Added **help text box** (`DefaultHelpArea`) (on the left side) optional **width adjustment** (negative value shrinks it). Make **x and y positions** (resolution-scaled), and **width** (hard pixel; not resolution-scaled) of the **unit bar** (`PlotListPanel`) **adjustable**, and **fix horizontal overflow of unit bar into scoreboard** when unit bar is full and scoreboard is hovered on (or toggle lock scoreboard hover is ON) (see [KI#124](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#124---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-map-view-unit-bar-overflows-into-hoveredexpanded-scoreboard)). Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**. Added a **Toggle show map annotations** (Alt + S **captions**, Alt + X **BFC marks**) button (next to the other buttons **above the Minimap**); the toggled state **persists on save and load**; reorganized buttons as part of this change (this takes the Event Log's former HUD icon former (it gets another one instead)). To accommodate this new minimap button's width, **reduce minimap buttons horizontal interspacing** so **last minimap button doesn't collide horizontally with globe view** button (except for squarish maps like as of now BTG_Cross, where this is a fine trade-off, and still improved significantly with this adjustment). See [README.md (Map annotations)](/README.md#map-annotations) and [KI#135](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#135---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-turn-status-text-collided-with-the-diplomacy-screen).
+- **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. Added **help text box** (`DefaultHelpArea`) (on the left side) optional **width adjustment** (negative value shrinks it). Make **x and y positions** (resolution-scaled), and **width** (hard pixel; not resolution-scaled) of the **unit bar** (`PlotListPanel`) **adjustable**, and **fix horizontal overflow of unit bar into scoreboard** when unit bar is full and scoreboard is hovered on (or toggle lock scoreboard hover is ON) (see [KI#124](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#124---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-map-view-unit-bar-overflows-into-hoveredexpanded-scoreboard)). Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**. Added a **Toggle show map annotations** (Alt + S **captions**, Alt + X **BFC marks**) button (next to the other buttons **above the Minimap**); the toggled state **persists on save and load**; reorganized buttons as part of this change (this takes the Event Log's former HUD icon former (it gets another one instead)). To accommodate this new minimap button's width, **reduce minimap buttons horizontal interspacing** so **last minimap button doesn't collide horizontally with globe view** button (except for squarish maps like as of now `BTG_Cross.py`, where this is a fine trade-off, and still improved significantly with this adjustment). See [README.md (Map annotations)](/README.md#map-annotations) and [KI#135](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#135---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-turn-status-text-collided-with-the-diplomacy-screen).
 **Scoreboard**: do **not draw beyond** bottom of commerce sliders (previously it would overflow beyond top of the screen), add **+** (up, fast up, and fastest up) and **-** (down, fast down, and fastest down (e.g., 1 by 1, 5 by 5, or 50 by 50 (effectively max))) **scroll buttons** to choose **first and last leader shown** when the **number of leaders is high** (e.g., if there are 48 leaders to display and the scoreboard can only show ~30 leaders max). Note: the Info screen's score tab allows to see all leaders so this is a fine trade-off to avoid vertical overflow. Add a **Toggle lock scoreboard hover button** so scoreboard is always hovered on even without hover (e.g., to see power ratios without having to hover). Note: in first turns of the game the lock button effectively has no effect since power ratios are not yet visible. Add a **Toggle Background Style button** (AdvCiv **default at each save load/new game kept**; tunable) (e.g., blue panel, black50, empty (transparent)). Change in [Scoreboard.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/Scoreboard.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [README.md (Scoreboard)](/README.md#scoreboard).
 - **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
 - **Worker recommendation highlights disabled**: turned off tile coloring for "worker-recommended plot to improve" (in `CvGame::updateColoredPlots` within `CvGameInterface.cpp`). Reasons: (1) avoids extra computation in both debug ([see for related info this autoplay info](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-autoplay-let-the-ai-play-for-you-super-fast-gameplay--testing-tool-in-map-loaded-save-file-new-game-etc-view)) and normal play; (2) our worker logic now relies on `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild`, so the vanilla highlight often disagrees and can mislead; (3) the highlight was easily confused with **city site** recommendations. City-site suggestions remain enabled and intentionally prominent; in practice, they frequently pick **strong** locations—quite often as good as, or better than, typical manual choices. See [Settlers (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#settlers-ai). *Note:* the **displayed recommended settle city plots** don’t always match what the AI would settle if it were playing your civ in autoplay; the UI hint path may be (not sure) using a different logic from the reworked/optimized `AIFoundValue::evaluate`. Treat them as general information, not guarantees.
